---
title: SQLSTATE Mapping
description: PostgreSQL-compatible SQLSTATE codes returned over pgwire.
---

# SQLSTATE Mapping

NodeDB maps internal error codes to PostgreSQL SQLSTATE codes for pgwire compatibility.

| NodeDB Error          | SQLSTATE | PostgreSQL Meaning           |
| --------------------- | -------- | ---------------------------- |
| Syntax error          | 42601    | Syntax error                 |
| Collection not found  | 42P01    | Undefined table              |
| Column not found      | 42703    | Undefined column             |
| Type mismatch         | 42846    | Cannot coerce                |
| Unique violation      | 23505    | Unique violation             |
| FK violation          | 23503    | Foreign key violation        |
| Check violation       | 23514    | Check violation              |
| Not null violation    | 23502    | Not null violation           |
| Permission denied     | 42501    | Insufficient privilege       |
| Numeric overflow      | 22003    | Numeric value out of range   |
| Division by zero      | 22012    | Division by zero             |
| Rate limit exceeded   | 53300    | Too many connections         |
| Tenant quota exceeded | 53400    | Configuration limit exceeded |
| Database quota exceeded | 53400  | Configuration limit exceeded |
| Server overload (`SERVER_OVERLOAD`, dispatch capacity) | 57P03 | Cannot connect now |
| Quota overcommit      | 53400    | Configuration limit exceeded |
| Database not found    | 3D000    | Invalid catalog name (HTTP 404) |
| Mirror read only      | 25006    | Read-only SQL transaction    |
| Stale read on mirror  | 55P03    | Lock not available (redirect to source) |
| Clone depth exceeded  | 54011    | Program limit exceeded (class 54) |
| Session not found     | 42704    | Undefined object             |
| Session idle timeout  | 42601    | Syntax error (`BAD_REQUEST`) |
| Session closed: user dropped or `KILL SESSION` | 42601 | Syntax error (`BAD_REQUEST`) |
| Internal error        | XX000    | Internal error               |

## Retryable capacity refusal (57P03)

`57P03` is a transient refusal. Its usual cause is a Data Plane dispatch queue at capacity: the server enqueued nothing and ran nothing. A collection that is draining and a migration in progress answer `57P03` too. Retry the same statement with backoff. See [Error Codes](./error-codes) for the full contract.
